      "created_at": "2017-11-21T08:34:33Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-11-21T08:34:33Z",
      "body": "Hello @jackjackde and thank you for using our module and submitting an issue.\r\n\r\nThe tracker does two things : \r\n\r\n- it collects data through a local domain (you are the only one having access to this data) about customer navigation (product view, bought, facet usage, etc...). This part is meant to be used later on our roadmap to build behavioral optimizers (boost most viewed products and things like this).\r\n\r\n- it sends a ping to a smile domain, with the url of the website using elasticsuite. Nothing more. It is just a way for us to track the module usage. Since it's published free and does not require any subscription or account anywhere to use it, it's a way for us to have statistics about the number of websites the module is deployed on.\r\n\r\nI hope to have answered your question. Do not hesitate if you want to know more.\r\n",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "pin": null,
