      "created_at": "2018-04-12T08:32:21Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-12T08:32:37Z",
      "body": "The tracker will be refactored in the 2.6 version, especially to be compliant with GDPR policy (we are in concern since we are a french company with mostly european customers) : \r\n\r\n- customer data tracking in Front-Office will require customer consent with a default and extendable implementation.\r\n\r\n- our internal tracking (the ping to t.smile.eu) will be moved inside adminhtml part exactly the same way than Magento is doing its own tracking with the AdminNotification module. Doing this will prevent us being asked about frontend/customer data tracking.\r\n\r\nBut I repeat, nothing belonging to the customer is tracked by the ping to t.smile.eu. We just collect the domain names where elasticsuite is deployed. I hope you'll understand this is the only way for us to measure the module usage, since we distribute it for free, and even with no registration needed anywhere.\r\n\r\nBest regards.",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "pin": null,
