      "updated_at": "2019-03-29T08:01:18Z",
      "body": "Hello.\r\n\r\nI'm not worried about Smile to get the data but I'm more worried that it sends on each customer request request to elasticsuite/tracker/hit/image/h.png which is executed thru Magento controller and adds one entry to elasticsuite_tracker_log_event and second to elasticsuite_tracker_log_customer_link .\r\n\r\nSimilar behaviour was on Magento's customer logging and is known bottleneck for performance issues.\r\n",
